WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.878 --> 00:00:01.711
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.711 --> 00:00:03.301
- Hi!

00:00:03.301 --> 00:00:04.134
Hi guys!

00:00:05.728 --> 00:00:06.561
Yes, yes!

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.350
And with that flower power,
I say to thee, guess what?

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.197
I fixed a toilet last night.

00:00:15.197 --> 00:00:16.030
(audience cheers)

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:16.863
Yes!

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:18.803
I did.

00:00:18.803 --> 00:00:21.820
Yeah, that's my Bruce Lee bada-bing.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.730
Listen, I felt like a man last night!

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.490
I did, because you know what?

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:29.840
Most of the time when
stuff like that happens,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.290
I'm like, oh, help me, oh God.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.300
But last night I was like, you know what?

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.850
Just lifted the lid off,
rolled up the sleeves,

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:40.737
went in, yanked the chain, reattached it.

00:00:40.737 --> 00:00:42.318
And it worked!

00:00:42.318 --> 00:00:43.151
(audience cheers)

00:00:43.151 --> 00:00:44.940
I know it's so silly, but...

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:49.724
You know, listen, we've all had to learn

00:00:49.724 --> 00:00:53.300
how to take care of
ourselves in a different way,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.020
because we're all stuck in our houses

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:56.470
and no one's around to help.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.580
So we gotta figure this out.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:02.610
And I wanna ask my BFFs,
has anyone else here

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.577
had a domestic Everest that they climbed?

00:01:05.577 --> 00:01:07.200
#DomesticEverest.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.033
Carly.

00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:11.170
- Hi.
- Hi Drew.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.170
- Hi ladies!

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:16.927
How are you?

00:01:18.347 --> 00:01:19.913
- Oh we're so excited.
- So excited.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.986
- Oh, you both look like
you're going to prom.

00:01:23.986 --> 00:01:24.888
I mean, I'm not kidding.

00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:26.530
- Wow.
- Thank you.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:27.363
- Gorgeous.

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.163
Did you guys have a domestic
Everest you climbed?

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.540
- Yes, yes, we recently moved
from Southern California

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.780
to Northern California and
I was missing the L.A. area.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.090
So I decided to remodel my master bedroom

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.550
to be more like an LA vibe.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:43.923
I did it all by myself.

00:01:45.372 --> 00:01:46.480
(audience claps)

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.160
- I mean, that really
is a domestic Everest.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.463
Mine was more like a domestic
Denali, maybe a Fuji.

00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:56.870
That is Everest, I am so impressed.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:57.940
Good for you, and thank you

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:02.790
for inspiring us to just
get it done, you know?

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.980
Thank you ladies, and you
could not look more beautiful.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.300
Okay, I am so excited for the show.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.330
We are talking to a woman
who's turned a cancer diagnosis

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.430
into a nationwide runners community.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.840
And I'm actually gonna try

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.941
and attempt to join this community myself.

00:02:18.941 --> 00:02:23.270
So I'm excited to present this
to all of you as an option.

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.650
And I'm also gonna step into the kitchen.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.880
I'm doing a cooking demo for a dish

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.470
that is very, very important to me,

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.550
and satiates something that
is sort of a naughty dish,

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.380
but I found a way to make it a nice dish.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:42.380
So first let's kick it
off with some Drew's News.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.420
We like to serve our
stories here sunny side up.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.033
It's Drew's News.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:48.866
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.866 --> 00:02:49.760
(car crashes)
(cat hisses)

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.233
Ma'am, I asked you a question.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.883
It's Drew's News!

00:02:56.851 --> 00:02:57.684
(audience cheers)

00:02:57.684 --> 00:03:00.530
I just really wanna thank our VFFs today,

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.760
because I felt so connected to everyone.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.100
I mean really, this is like
an awesome crowd today,

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.400
and every day here is, with our VFFs.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.370
I love hanging out with everyone.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.580
All right, let's kick
it off with the news.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.340
We try to find the good little morsels

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.700
that carry us throughout the day.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:23.180
It's time for history, herstory!

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.870
Herstory football!

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.340
That's right, this Sunday
for the first time ever,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.980
three women were on the field
at an official NFL game, okay?

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.560
Yeah, that happened.
(audience claps)

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.360
At the Washington/Cleveland game

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.420
there was one female coach for each team,

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.930
and one female referee
officiating the game,

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:48.301
Callie Brownson, Jennifer
King and Sarah Thomas.

00:03:48.301 --> 00:03:49.510
(audience cheers)

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:52.230
I love this story.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.850
This herstory!

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.783
Thank you ladies, making us all look good.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.980
Okay, next up in the news,

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:02.330
it's a story that your stomach cares about

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.670
because it's food news.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:05.742
- [Woman] Nom, nom, nom, nom.

00:04:05.742 --> 00:04:10.100
- (laughs) Delish.com reports that Nabisco

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.595
has released their limited
edition Maple Cream Oreo.

00:04:14.595 --> 00:04:18.830
And it's two golden cookies
with maple syrup flavor,

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:20.910
stuffed with the traditional Oreo cream

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:21.750
we all know and love.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:24.450
I mean, if it didn't have
that, it wouldn't be an Oreo.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.390
So I wanna try this.

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:31.040
I met a really fun friend
in the VFF Wall, Jason,

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.370
and I asked him to come
back here, actually.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.250
We did a turkey dinner
candy corn taste test

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.470
last week, and I loved his review.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.430
So I'm bringing him back.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.712
Jason, how are ya?

00:04:43.712 --> 00:04:47.160
- Hi Drew, hello, I'm great.
- Hi.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.480
- Thank you for having me.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.960
- I just was like, we
all love you so much.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.670
We were like, will Jason come back?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.311
So thank you.
- I did.

00:04:55.311 --> 00:04:58.863
- You came back, Jason,
how do you rock an Oreo?

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:03.220
- You know, I just, old-school fashion.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.320
Just a little milk.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.840
You know, I let it sit in
there for a little bit,

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.810
then I take it out and eat it.

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.680
But yeah, a little milk.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.890
I don't have milk for today.

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.350
- I was just gonna say,
now I'm so disappointed.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:15.750
I should've...

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.820
Next time we will have
a cold milk standing by.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.225
Okay, so shall we taste test these?

00:05:22.225 --> 00:05:23.230
You ready?

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.106
- Let's do it, here we go.
- Cheers.

00:05:25.106 --> 00:05:25.939
- Cheers.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.137
(audience laughs)

00:05:35.137 --> 00:05:36.630
- Me likey.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.963
- That's fall.
- Yeah.

00:05:39.421 --> 00:05:40.254
- That's fall in a cookie.

00:05:40.254 --> 00:05:43.890
- It's also like IHOP in your mouth.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.147
- Yeah.

00:05:45.147 --> 00:05:50.147
- It's like maple syrup,
Vermont party right here.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.120
- Yeah, like I can't go to Canada anymore,

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.090
because they won't let us in.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:58.320
So I'm just gonna eat these instead.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:01.620
- Yeah, you got your
maple leaf right here.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:02.714
- Oh, that's perfect.

00:06:02.714 --> 00:06:05.330
- Oh my god, these are
really good, I'm not kidding.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.783
They have almost like that maple smoke,

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.983
it's beautiful, wow.

00:06:13.909 --> 00:06:15.440
All right, we have to move on.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.160
Okay, that's really hard to put down.

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.783
All right, Jason, do you have the samosas?

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.190
- I have them right here.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:24.450
And this has been very
difficult all morning

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.572
because they have smelled so good.

00:06:26.572 --> 00:06:30.050
- They're kind of one of my
favorite treats in the world.

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:33.540
Fun fact, they are a
savory Indian puff pastry

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.380
filled with potatoes and vegetables.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:39.050
And it's one of my favorite things to eat.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:43.650
And this one has a pumpkin spiced samosa.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:46.530
Trader Joe's just released this pairing

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.973
that made me go, oh my gourd.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:52.403
Here we go, ready?
- Let's do it.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:58.580
- Oh my god, oh my god.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.936
- I didn't expect that,

00:06:59.936 --> 00:07:01.580
did not expect that.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:03.545
- That is so good.

00:07:03.545 --> 00:07:05.370
- That is delicious, spicy too.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.660
- And the pumpkin really worked

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.479
'cause you already are
used to like a potato vibe.

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:11.320
- Yeah.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.970
- By the way, Trader Joe's food reviews

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:16.630
on Instagram, are you on that, Jason?

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.048
Anyone?

00:07:18.048 --> 00:07:20.270
It's the best, it's
really good, get on it.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.270
- I will get on it today.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:23.423
- Oh my god, this is so amazing.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:25.923
- Thank you, Jason.

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:31.910
From VFF to FFF, favorite
foodie friend forever.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.918
That might be four Fs.

00:07:33.918 --> 00:07:36.501
(upbeat music)

